<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Constructing a cubic with given turning points</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Give an equation of a cubic curve that has a maximum point at \(x = {@p0@}\) and a minimum point at \(x = {@q0@}\).</p><p>Think about what \(\dfrac{dy}{dx}\) must be.</p><div>\(y =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Stationary points are where \(\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 0\), so \(\dfrac{dy}{dx}\) must have the factors \({@x-p0@}\) and \({@x-q0@}\). One choice is \(\dfrac{dy}{dx} = {@6*s0*(x-p0)*(x-q0)@} = {@dsamp@}\), which gives</p><p>\[y = {@samp@}\]</p><p>Check: \(\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} = {@diff(samp,x,2)@}\), which is \({@ev(diff(samp,x,2),x=p0)@}\) at \(x = {@p0@}\) (negative: a maximum point) and \({@ev(diff(samp,x,2),x=q0)@}\) at \(x = {@q0@}\) (positive: a minimum point).</p><p>Any \(y = k\left({@samp@}\right) + c\) with \(k \gt 0\) also works.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_poly(ex) := if not every(lambda([v], member(v, [x])), listofvars(ex)) then "Use x as the only letter in your answer." elseif not polynomialp(ev(ex,simp),[x]) then "Your answer should be a polynomial in x: powers of x only, with no other functions." else "";
/* Design: construct-an-example pattern (the response tree checks properties; many correct answers). The box takes polynomials in x only (validate_poly), because an answer such as cubic + cos(pi x) would pass every property test. Source: original. */
L: [[-1,2],[3,1],[0,4],[-2,1],[2,-1],[-3,0],[1,5],[4,-2],[-1,-4],[5,2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
p0: L[ix][1]; q0: L[ix][2];
s0: if p0<q0 then 1 else -1;
samp: expand((2*s0)*x^3-3*(2*s0)*((p0)+(q0))/2*x^2+3*(2*s0)*(p0)*(q0)*x+(0));
dsamp: diff(samp,x);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, max at {@p0@}, min at {@q0@}, sample {@samp@}</text>
  </questionnote>
